course: dictionary
lesson: 13372
title: Hauling: pulling and carrying
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hauling means pulling or dragging something heavy with effort. It can also mean carrying goods by lorry or truck from place to place. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «The fishermen spent all morning hauling in the nets» tells you they were pulling heavy nets, not carrying them.
explain: «The crane was hauling the steel beams up to the roof.» The clues are crane, steel and roof. A crane lifts heavy things, and beams are large and heavy, so hauling means lifting or pulling something heavy with effort. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word.
explain: Sometimes hauling is used in an informal way. «Dad said, "I am hauling you off to bed now!"» Nobody is dragging a sack here. It means taking someone somewhere they do not want to go. The word «hauling» is a little playful in that sentence.
fact: Hauling means pulling or dragging something heavy with effort.
fact: Hauling can also mean carrying goods by lorry or truck from place to place. The job itself is called hauling, and it is a noun.
fact: «The men were hauling the sacks up the hill.» Here hauling means dragging heavy things with effort.
fact: In informal speech, «hauling» means taking someone somewhere they do not want to go, as in «hauling them off to the dentist».
fact: Hauling is a verb. Its other forms are haul, hauls and hauled.
exercise: «The fishermen spent all morning hauling in the nets.» What is hauling here? | Singing a happy song | Cooking fish for lunch | Sleeping on the boat | *Pulling something heavy with effort
exercise: Pat wants a job hauling goods across the country. What does hauling mean in that sentence? | Selling ice cream on the beach | Building houses from bricks | Teaching children to swim | *Carrying goods by lorry or truck from place to place
exercise: Dad said, «I am hauling you off to bed now!» What does hauling suggest? | Carrying you gently in his arms | Pulling a heavy sack up the stairs | *Taking you somewhere you do not want to go
test: Mia's uncle works in hauling. What is his job? | Painting houses | Working as a baker | *Carrying goods by lorry or truck from place to place | Fishing for crabs
test: Which word could replace hauling in «The men were hauling the sacks up the hill»? | singing | forgetting | dropping | *dragging
exam: Which sentence uses hauling in the informal way? | *Grandma is hauling me to the shop, though I hate shopping. | The lorry driver is hauling cement to the city. | The sailors were hauling the net in.
